WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.600
…so that you can present it at your restaurant.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.200
Now we take out the tortillas, which are ready and golden,
and let them drain.

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.800
We don't want them to be too greasy.

4
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:31.600
And now let's check our chicken,
which should be ready.

5
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:42.000
We cut it into small cubes

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.800
so it looks good on the plate.

7
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.800
The chicken can be cut to any size,
depending on the dish.

8
00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.200
Some people use very large dishes;
others use slightly smaller ones.

9
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.200
Some sell it in what they call cups,
others in bowls,

10
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.400
but this is the ideal dish:
one that holds 8 ounces of water,

11
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:17.000
just one dish, so restaurants also have the chance
to sell other products,

12
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.400
and customers don't fill up on just one item.

13
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:27.600
There's our chicken. Next we add the cheese.

14
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:35.800
I recommend Monterey Jack, mozzarella, or any kind
of cheese that melts well.

15
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.400
If it doesn't melt well, it won't give the chicken
the same texture or the same flavor.

16
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:50.000
I can leave a little strip on top,
so it shows a bit and looks better.

17
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:57.800
We're going to add two slices of avocado.

18
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:03.400
You can also use just one slice
if you cut it into small pieces.

19
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:11.000
It looks better with two slices, but we also know
that avocado is expensive most of the year.

20
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:17.800
For this presentation, I'll use two slices
so it looks good.

21
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.000
And finally, we're going to add the broth,

22
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.200
the broth, nice and hot, boiling,

23
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.800
so the cheese melts nicely.

24
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.800
Now we can serve it at the table
as soon as it's ready.

25
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.000
And there you have it.

26
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.600
Enjoy!

